1. Domains that I used GitHub Copilot for

I used GitHub Copilot to assist in several areas, including:

Technical research (e.g., understanding Okta SPA vs Backend authentication flow)
Migrating application components from Struts to Spring MVC
Developing Playwright automated test cases
Resolving SonarQube and Prisma findings
Implementing AKS health probes and Health APIs
Implementing Security Audit Logging
Code refactoring, debugging, and documentation
Develop APIs to integrate with different applications


2. Velocity of adaptation / learning curve

Medium

Getting started with GitHub Copilot was relatively easy. With clear prompts, it can provide useful suggestions for coding, technical research, and troubleshooting.

However, using Copilot effectively takes more practice. Writing better prompts, refining responses, validating generated code, and minimizing token usage are skills to improve over time. 

3. Measurement of business benefits
GitHub Copilot helped reduce the time spent on technical research, repetitive coding, and issue remediation, allowing more time to focus on other project activities.

It supported work such as:

Okta implementation research
